  "id": "COMPOUND:30353 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 3-(Methylthio)-2-butanone and HepG2 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The compound is implicated in targeting Tankyrase-2, which is a key enzyme involved in various cellular processes, including DNA repair and cell proliferation. Tankyrase-2 is also a target of multiple compounds, including Cocosamide B and Tubotaiwine, both of which have been shown to interact with HepG2 cells. Similarly, 5-O-Methylcelebixanthone, another compound targeting Tankyrase-2, also shows a connection to HepG2. These findings collectively indicate that 3-(Methylthio)-2-butanone may exert its biological effects through the modulation of Tankyrase-2, which in turn influences HepG2 cell behavior. The consistent involvement of Tankyrase-2 as a common target across different compounds supports a mechanistic link between the compound and HepG2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
